{"schema_version":"cera.scene_writer_draft.v1","story_text":"The entryway held the last of the evening's cool air, a faint draft slipping in before Ted shut the door behind him. Hana stood with her hands clasped loosely in front of her, the soft light from the hallway catching the warmth in her expression. A few steps back, Mia lingered near the coat rack, hands tucked into her pockets, gaze drifting between them without pressing forward.\n\nHana tilted her head slightly, a small smile curving her lips. \"Dinner went well,\" she said, her voice carrying a gentle, unhurried warmth. The words hung there, simple and complete, as the quiet of the entryway settled around them.\n\nTed stood just inside the door, the moment open before him."}